    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d664">

                <pb facs="0761" n="641" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.002 Mtissolini/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Italian Premier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mussolini</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Italian Ambassador in the
                        United States</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">De Martino</hi>)<anchor n="28"
                        xml:id="d664-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-30T14:00:00+01:00">January 30, 1931—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 30—9 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your telegrams 88 and 89. I felt sure that I would obtain just and prompt redress
                    from the fairness, the loyalty and the friendship of the <pb facs="0762" n="642"
                        xml:id="pg642"/> American Government and the American people whose respect
                    for truth is well known to me. Will you please communicate to the Federal
                    Government that I consider closed the incident which for my part I have already
                    forgotten. After making this communication to the American Government Your
                    Excellency may give the press this text.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mussolini</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d664-f1" n="28" type="source" xml:id="d664-f1-content">
                <p>Text in English handed to the Secretary of State by the Italian Ambassador,
                    January 30, 1931.</p>
            </note>
